sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor S as Student
    participant B as Browser (Monaco editor)
    participant G as Gateway
    participant AS as assessment-service
    participant CX as codeexec-service
    participant SB as Judge0 / Piston

    Note over S,SB: Practice editor in a lesson
    S->>B: write code, choose language (if the author allowed it)
    B->>G: POST /api/code/run {language, source, stdin}
    G->>CX: forward (45 s timeout)
    CX->>CX: signed in? language enabled? size ok? per-user rate limit, concurrency cap
    CX->>SB: run with time, memory limits, no network
    SB-->>CX: output / compile error / runtime error / timeout
    CX-->>B: outcome
    B->>G: POST /api/code/analyze
    CX->>CX: static analysis: lines, nesting, loops, complexity estimate
    CX-->>B: metrics, explanation, optimisation hints, growth chart

    Note over S,SB: Coding question inside a test
    S->>B: Run tests
    B->>G: POST /quiz-attempts/{id}/questions/{q}/run-tests (90 s, no circuit breaker)
    G->>AS: forward
    AS->>AS: enforce the allowed language server-side
    AS->>CX: run the test cases (CodeClient, /api/code/run-batch)
    CX->>SB: each case
    SB-->>CX: result per case with time and memory
    CX-->>AS: verdict list
    AS->>AS: store verdict + SHA-256 of the code, a refused run keeps the old verdict
    AS-->>B: passed / failed per test case

    S->>B: Submit test
    B->>AS: submit
    AS->>AS: changed code is re-run, marks come from the stored verdict
    Note over AS: scoring never runs code itself,<br/>so the expiry job needs no token
